supplies do not sum to zero, or some set of vertices supplies more than its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out-edges carry. Costs may be negative; negative cycles are saturated (capacities are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"finite). A self-loop carries its capacity when its cost is negative and nothing otherwise.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Network simplex with block-search pivots and strongly feasible trees, LEMON’s layout.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"supply"},{"text":" is called once per vertex in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"text":" order, then, for each edge in position","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"text":" and then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cost"},{"text":", before any work. Which optimum is returned when several","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exist is unspecified, but the same input always gives the same result.","type":"text"}],"title":"minimumCostFlow(supply:capacity:cost:)"},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/edgeDisjointPaths(from:to:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/edgedisjointpaths(from:to:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/edgeDisjointPaths(from:to:)","kind":"symbol","title":"edgeDisjointPaths(from:to:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"edgeDisjointPaths","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"t